    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (80.32) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (78.09). **Yordan Alvarez** faces Rea in a matchup that maximizes his elite xwOBA, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains our primary engine for stolen bases; his 14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against Teng makes him a must-start despite the moderate SP skill of the opposition. **Christian Yelich** also earns a top-tier rating (74.32) tonight, as the combination of Sasaki\u2019s 5.11 xERA and a significant platoon edge allows him to provide elite offensive production that is difficult to fade in 5x5 formats.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical constraints in today\u2019s construction. While **Trea Turner** (68.34) and **Kyle Schwarber** (64.05) remain strong plays, both are slightly dampened by wind blowing in, which offsets the value of their prime spots at the top of the order against Cecconi. The toughest decision involved our bench; **Kazuma Okamoto** was the most notable exclusion, as his projection was completely neutralized by an unfavorable matchup against Skenes (2.96 xERA) and his current status outside the active starting lineup. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** was removed from consideration entirely due to a rainout. We are comfortable rolling with **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Casey Schmitt**, and **Carson Benge** in the remaining slots, though we will keep a close eye on the late-breaking lineup data for **Casey Schmitt**, whose value is sensitive to his position in the batting order. We are essentially punting marginal gains in the bottom-third of the order to preserve our game caps, ensuring that assets like **Colt Keith**, **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena** remain fresh for higher-leverage matchups later in the week.",
